====== Edimax NS-1500N ======

Tested with a modified fonera 2.0n openwrt firmware image. 

Usb, wifi, lan, all seem to work.


It uses the Ralink RT3050 SoC, wifi drivers are binary and only work with 2.6.21 kernel, so don't expect latest trunk to be stable for while yet.

===== Hardware Highlights =====
^ CPU       ^ Ram    ^ Flash   ^ Network   ^ USB   ^ Serial   ^ JTAG   ^
| RT3050F   | 32MB   | 8MB     | 1         | Yes   | Yes      | No     |

===== Installation =====

This is more of an FYI than a guide as its very ghetto and could potential brick your device YOU HAVE BEEN WARNED.

I recommend backing up your firmware if you do attempt flashing as there are no recovery images available. 


I've only tested installing firmware via serial.

Pressing 2 while Uboot starts lets you flash an image via tftp.

I used the fonera 2.0n build system to produce a fon/openwrt firware. 

The only requirements to get it to boot is editing the kernel config for 32mb RAM and the RT3050.

